# Code owners. The main-protection ruleset requires code-owner review, so a PR touching a path
# below cannot merge without approval from that owner.
#
# CODEOWNERS and .github/ (workflows, actions) are listed so the protection itself, and anything
# that runs with repo secrets or publishes, can't be changed without the owner. Repo-wide review
# of what else belongs here is tracked in a separate issue.

/.github/ @IanMStevenson

# The b-oss website: published at b-oss.dev, and stubs/ holds the permanent redirects that released
# b-mobile builds and store listings depend on.
/packages/b-site/ @IanMStevenson

# docs/ was the old GitHub Pages source (the site now lives in packages/b-site). Keep it owner-only
# so nothing is quietly published from it or recreated by accident.
/docs/ @IanMStevenson
